# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the op-fusion programme's M1 package (matmul grids for the 13x10 compute grid; docs/tp4-fusion-m1.md): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the fusion integration branch (with fusion-wp/M1.json placed by make_fusion_profiles.py --write and fusion-wp/M1-tp-addresses.patch applied) and
# push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its
# author. M1/ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag the pack's B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# M1A (EXACTNESS, M1): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-grid13-audit = the audited combined fusion arm (c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-audit: every integrated lever and its audit) plus QWEN_FAST_GRID13=1 and QWEN_FAST_GRID13_AUDIT=1. The smoke runs the warm-up (the eager prefill warm
# runs every prefill all-gather matmul and the eager verify warm every 64-row projection on the lever, then again on the served config beside it, and compares every chip's bytes), the SOLO prefill ladder
# (four real-code prompts of about 4,096 / 32,768 / 131,072 / 253,920 tokens, one request at a time: TTFT and prefill rate of each rung, the lever in every chunk) and eight live. C2_TELEMETRY=1: the
# read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second (AICLK under load, power, temperature, throttlers), which says whether a gain is real or the clocks moved.
# READ: c2_smoke_check clean with the fusion rules and the M1 rule (grid13_smoke: an engaged line for site=gdn_in, site=attn_in, the MLP's site and site=verify.out, a passing audit line
# `[PINDIAG] tp4 grid13 audit n=<n> exact=True site=<site>` for each, no fell-back line, no 'audit mismatch'), the existing combined-arm audits as in the combined pack's FXA, every answer complete, no stall.
# ANY mismatch, fall-back, missing engaged line or missing audit line is NO-GO for the lever and skips its timed jobs. A hang or a program error at the first prefill (a 12-wide minimal matmul at M block 6 never
# ran on a card before this job) is the card telling the 12x6 plan is not legal: read the log for the op's own refusal, then repeat with QWEN_FAST_GRID13_CFG=agmm=10 (10 wide, 5 workers a link) or agmm=12x4 (the
# served M block) in a copy of the profile before declaring the lever dead.
# Duration (estimate): 80 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-grid13-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,prefill_ladder_solo,concurrent8_steady
C2_BOX_MINUTES=120
C2_TELEMETRY=1
